**Ladder and decisions**
- With no peer known, a chat request goes straight to the plain bridge. Otherwise the local floor runs first.
- A refusal from the local floor before any body byte (404, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504, 508) triggers one peer attempt. If no peer takes it, the local refusal is replayed unchanged.
- If the floor has not answered within `localQueueMs` (default 10 s), a peer is asked in parallel and the first byte wins.
- Peers go first only when the floors answered, none holds the model, no fleet tab serves it, and a peer is eligible.
- Only `/api/chat` and `/api/generate` use the peer ladder. `/v1/*` and `/api/job` stay local-only.
- The bridge's own `/status` moved to `/heimdall/bridge-status`, because `/heimdall/status` is now `HeimdallEmbed@1`.
- If you inject `stateDir`, the peer token defaults to `<stateDir>/peers.token`, so two such instances cannot peer unless you also pass `peerTokenFile` or `peerToken`. Otherwise it is the shared `~/.heimdall/peers.token`.
